        <!-- The focused item's zoom is a bigger focusedlayout box rather
             than a container-level Focus/UnFocus animation, so it can't
             zoom the whole row - just the hovered poster. The box only
             grows rightward/vertically, never leftward: Kodi can't scroll a
             horizontal list to a negative offset, so any leftward overflow
             on the list's first item is unrenderable no matter how much
             margin the list control is given (confirmed this also affects
             the already-shipped Search screen's leftmost result - it's a
             Kodi limitation, not a margin-sizing bug). The list's own
             declared box is grown 30px top/bottom (posy raised, height
             increased) since Kodi clips a list's content - including zoom
             overflow - to the list control's own posy/height, not its
             parent group's; growing only the enclosing group (tried in
             0.3.60) left the list's real clip region unchanged. Unfocused
             posters are sized a few px smaller than the focused box
             (257x387 vs 288x430) so the focused item visibly "pops". -->
